Dependencies

The published npm package carries more than the above: its player bundles the
npm packages listed in its `inlinedDependencies`, and its WebAssembly bake is
compiled from Rust crates (resvg, tiny-skia, parley, skrifa, ravif, rav1e,
image-webp, zip, ruzstd, serde and others), most of them under the MIT,
Apache-2.0 or BSD licences. Their names, authors, licences and licence texts are
in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md, at the root of the npm package: it is written by
`pnpm --filter folioscope build:wasm` from the crates Cargo resolved for that
build, so it always matches the binary it ships with. `cargo deny check` keeps
the licences of the Rust dependencies within those the AGPL allows.
